    "5-17-4-1": {
      "status": "na",
      "reason": "This is a limit on the physical token supply checked while preparing to play (six or fewer copies per token card number). The simulator creates token instances from card data when they are needed (the same reason 6-1-2-1 is N/A), and decklists never contain tokens, so there is no supply to validate. How many copies can be in play at once is already capped by 11-4-1 (six Units), 4-4-2-1 (five EX Resources) and 11-5-1 (one Base), and those rules are tested separately."
    },
    "5-17-4-3": {
      "status": "na",
      "reason": "The simulator has no face-down token supply prepared before the game. The only token instances outside the game are ones that left a public location (battle area, base section or resource area), so both players already saw them. There are no unrevealed token contents for the information model (engine/observe.py) to hide. The public count of tokens outside the game (5-17-4-2) is tested."
    },
    "5-17-4-4": {
      "status": "na",
      "reason": "This only permits a player to set aside tokens they will not use while preparing to play. Tokens are created when needed, so unused tokens never exist and no game state depends on them."
    },
